// expect-error: NITPICK-TYPE-046
// expect-error-at: 18:5
// 2026-11-19 (landing 177d2d, row 10: the Bridge, form BR-5g, closing DEF-704, DEF-705, DEF-706, DEF-707 and DEF-712; rulings l.18410, l.19234,
// l.19307, l.19443, l.20202 and l.20254). A stub takes its bulk offset from the Bridge's own `ring_cap`, never from the region (DEF-704); refuses a
// call whose slots, slice bytes or return word don't fit the bulk area, as `OutOfBounds`, before any write (DEF-705); checks `closed` and `poisoned`
// first (DEF-706); `dispatch` range-checks the driver's indices before any arithmetic and kills a driver that rewrote line 0 (DEF-707); close and the
// reap clear the base and the stderr tail's cursor, and the tail refuses a closed Bridge (DEF-706, DEF-712); and every field of `Shm` and `Bridge` is
// `sealed` (D-313; DEF-467's fix for these two structs, l.19307). a probe of the seal (l.19443 item 1): a generic whole copy, TYPE-046, on main as
// here. From seat AB's release hunt on BR-5f and BR-5g (l.19307, l.19443), `Team/TMP/atk-177d2d-bridge-2026-11-19/cells/ab/`, `seal_generic.npk`, by
// `cat`, its `mod:` line and library path changed.
// seat AB (Ailp-team_215), 2026-11-19, seal route (generic): a generic whole-struct copy instantiated at `Bridge`.
// If the move-only / seal check fires only on the generic body and is skipped at monomorphization, this would let a
// program overwrite a Bridge's sealed fields through the generic (a whole-struct store). No `wild` keyword.
mod:bridge_seal_generic;
use "../../../lib/nbridge.npk".*;

func:gcopy<T> = NIL(T->:a, T->:c) never fails {
    <-a = <-c;
    pass NIL;
};

func:caller = NIL(Bridge->:a, Bridge->:c) {
    drop gcopy::<Bridge>(a, c);
    pass NIL;
};

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) { exit 0i32; };
func:failsafe = int32(Error:_~e) { exit 1i32; };
